## Approach

Port ~23 pure-math functions from swephlib.c into `src/math.rs` as a flat module of free functions, following the pattern established by `src/date.rs`. Use raw `[f64; 3]` and `[f64; 6]` arrays for coordinate vectors (per design decision). Match C floating-point math exactly — use `%` operator (≡ C `fmod`) not `rem_euclid`, preserve near-zero guards — to satisfy the bitwise golden-data mandate.

